  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"13a(i, ii, &amp;amp; iii)\"><p><strong>13a(i, ii, &amp;amp; iii)</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"13b(i)\"><p><strong>13b(i)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Net force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"= 2 \\times \\frac{(8.99 \\times 10^{9})(28 \\times 10^{-6})(56 \\times 10^{-6})}{0.5^{2}} \\times cos(45^\\circ) \\approx 80\"></span> N</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"13b(ii)\"><p><strong>13b(ii)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Electric field at P due to the negative charges:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2 \\times \\frac{(8.99 \\times 10^{9})(28 \\times 10^{-6})}{0.373^{2}} \\times cos\\left ( \\frac{143^{\\circ}}{2} \\right ) \\approx 1.15 \\times 10^{6}\"></span> N C<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Electric field at P due to the positive charge:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{(8.99 \\times 10^{9})(56 \\times 10^{-6})}{0.236^{2}} \\approx 9.04 \\times 10^{6}\"></span> N C<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Total electric field at P:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.15 \\times 10^{6} + 9.04 \\times 10^{6} \\approx 10.2 \\times 10^{6}\"></span> N C<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Three point charges are held at the vertices of a right-angled isosceles triangle. P is a point inside the triangle.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. On the diagram, draw an arrow to represent:</p>\n<p>i. the direction of the electric force on the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"+2Q\"></span> charge due to the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-Q\"></span> charge that is held at vertex A. Label this arrow with the letter F.</p>\n<p>  [1]</p>\n<p>ii. the direction of the net electric force that acts on the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"+2Q\"></span> charge. Label this arrow with the letter T.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>iii. the direction of the electric field at point P. Label this arrow with the letter E.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>b. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q = 28 \\: \\mu\"></span>C.</p>\n<p>Calculate:</p>\n<p>i. the magnitude of the net force that acts on the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"+2Q\"></span> charge.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p>ii. The magnitude of the electric field at point P.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>"
  },
